.\" Manual page for ci-bill. Wording of the options follows the binary --help text.
.TH CI-BILL 1
.nh
.SH NAME
ci-bill \- rank GitHub Actions cost per workflow from the billing usage CSV and point to likely causes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ci-bill [-h | --help] [-V | --version] <command> [arguments]
ci-bill report [options] --usage <CSV>
ci-bill prices [options]
ci-bill fetch [options] --repo <OWNER/REPO> --out <DIR> --since <DATE>
ci-bill help [command]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rank GitHub Actions cost per workflow from the billing usage CSV and point to likely causes.
.PP
.B report
ranks cost from a detailed usage report.
It requires --usage.
--runs is optional.
Together with the usage CSV it adds measured, per-job cost on top of the invoice.
--workflows reads workflow YAML (including reusable workflows and composite actions) and points at likely causes.
--usage and --runs are not alternatives:
.B report
without --usage exits 3.
.PP
.B prices
prints the built-in Actions runner price table, or the USD-per-minute rate for one label or SKU.
It makes no network connection.
.PP
.B fetch
saves a repository's Actions runs, jobs, and referenced reusable workflows into a directory that --runs reads.
It is the only command that uses the network.
Set GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN in the environment (the first one set is sent).
An optional GITHUB_API_URL must be an http or https URL; the default is https://api.github.com.
.PP
.B help
prints this command list, the same text as --help.
ci-bill help report prints the options for report (the same text as ci-bill report --help).
The same form works for prices and fetch.
help takes command names, not flags:
ci-bill help --help is an unrecognized subcommand and exits 3.
.PP
.B report
and
.B prices
are offline.
Only usage rows whose product is
.I actions
are ranked.
Other products are summed as one total and are not broken down per repository or workflow.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Top-level"
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version.
Accepted only on the top-level command.
A subcommand rejects --version.
.TP
.B --quiet
Hide the
.B what to do
line, even when stderr is a terminal.
No context line.
Accepted on
.BR report ,
.BR prices ,
and
.B fetch
as well.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print the
.B what to do
line, and on success one context line on stderr, even when stderr is a pipe.
Accepted on
.BR report ,
.BR prices ,
and
.B fetch
as well.
.SS report
Rank workflow costs from a detailed usage report.
.PP
Usage: ci-bill report [options] --usage <CSV>
.TP
.B --usage <CSV>
Detailed usage report CSV.
`-' reads standard input.
.TP
.B --workflows <DIR>
Directory of workflow YAML files.
.TP
.B --runs <DIR>
Saved Actions API JSON (`runs-*.json' and `jobs-<run_id>*.json') and cached remote workflows at `<owner>/<repo>/<path>@<ref>'.
.TP
.B --top <N>
Show the N workflows with the highest net amount.
.TP
.B --json
Print one JSON object instead of the text report.
.TP
.B --budget <AMOUNT>
Net total budget in USD.
Exit 1 when the total is above this.
.TP
.B --fix-diff
Print a unified diff fixing the highest-savings finding instead of the report.
.TP
.B --md
Print a one-page Markdown teardown instead of the report.
.TP
.B --output <PATH>
Write the report to this file instead of standard output.
An existing file is replaced.
If the parent directory does not exist, the command exits 1 and does not create it.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.SS prices
Show Actions runner prices and the minute rate for a label or SKU.
.PP
Usage: ci-bill prices [options]
.TP
.B --json
Print one JSON object instead of the text table.
.TP
.B --runner-map <CSV>
CSV of `label,sku' rows.
Matching labels use this SKU instead of the built-in map.
`-' reads standard input (not if --usage is also `-').
.TP
.B --label <LABEL>
Runner label or list, for example `ubuntu-latest' or `[self-hosted, macos]'.
.TP
.B --sku <SKU>
Actions SKU.
With --label, it must be the SKU that label resolves to.
.TP
.B --usage <CSV>
Detailed usage report.
Own rows for the workflow and SKU replace the table rate.
`-' reads standard input (not if --runner-map is also `-').
.TP
.B --repository <OWNER/REPO>
Repository (`owner/repo') that owns the usage rows.
.TP
.B --workflow <PATH>
Workflow path inside the usage report.
.TP
.B --output <PATH>
Write the report to this file instead of standard output.
An existing file is replaced.
If the parent directory does not exist, the command exits 1 and does not create it.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.PP
--workflow requires --usage.
--repository requires --usage.
--usage requires --label or --sku.
--usage and --runner-map cannot both read standard input.
.SS fetch
Save Actions runs, jobs, and referenced reusable workflows.
.PP
Usage: ci-bill fetch [options] --repo <OWNER/REPO> --out <DIR> --since <DATE>
.TP
.B --repo <OWNER/REPO>
Repository to read, as `OWNER/REPO'.
.TP
.B --out <DIR>
Directory for `repo.json', `runs-*.json', `jobs-<run_id>*.json', and callee files.
.TP
.B --since <DATE>
First day to fetch, as `YYYY-MM-DD' in UTC.
.TP
.B --until <DATE>
Last day to fetch, as `YYYY-MM-DD' in UTC.
Defaults to today.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.PP
--repo, --out, and --since are required.
--until before --since is a usage error.
A missing GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN is a usage error.
.SS help
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s).
.PP
Usage: ci-bill help [command]...
.PP
Arguments: one or more command names.
Prints help for those subcommands.
With no names, prints the top-level help.
This command has no long options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including --help and --version.
A closed stdout pipe (a reader that exits early) is also success.
.TP
.B 1
--budget was set and the Actions net total is above it, or the report could not be written (stdout for a reason other than a closed pipe, or --output; for example a full disk or a missing parent directory).
.TP
.B 2
An input could not be used: missing column, a value that is not a number, invalid YAML or JSON, an unreadable file, a file or standard input larger than 268435456 bytes (256 MiB), an unknown SKU, or
.B fetch
could not use the GitHub API (network, HTTP status, rejected token, or rate limit).
.TP
.B 3
Usage error: unknown option, missing required flag, an invalid --budget amount, a runner label that is not in the price table, disagreeing
.B prices
flags, or a
.B fetch
usage error such as a missing token, a bad date, or --until before --since.
.TP
.B 130
SIGINT.
The report is not left half-written.
An existing
.B --output
file is kept when the new report was not finished, and nothing is written to stdout.
Stderr is
.BR "ci-bill: interrupted by SIGINT" .
A
.B fetch
that has not published its cache yet leaves that cache as it was.
Exit codes 0, 1, 2 and 3 are unchanged.
.SH EXAMPLES
The CSV below is not installed with the binary.
It lives in the source tree and is invented.
.PP
.nf
ci-bill report --usage examples/usage.csv
.fi
.PP
Exits 0.
.PP
.nf
ci-bill prices
ci-bill --version
ci-bill --help
ci-bill help report
.fi
.PP
Each of those exits 0.
.PP
.nf
ci-bill report --usage no-such-usage.csv
.fi
.PP
Exits 2.
.PP
An unknown option exits 3, and the message is a usage error rather than a panic.
